From: CoreRouter <noreply@corerouter.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wpa_supplicant: ask for a new scan after an aborted one

A scan for a network to connect to that the kernel aborts (the interface
went down and up again under it, as when it is enslaved to a bond, which
takes its slaves down) reaches _wpa_supplicant_event_scan_results() with
scan_info.aborted set. The results are rightly not used, but nothing asks
for another scan either: wpa_state stays WPA_SCANNING and the station never
connects again until something else happens to the interface.

Seen in the CoreRouter bonding lab (two mac80211_hwsim station-bridges
enslaved to a bond while scanning): one of the two stayed in SCANNING for
good ("nl80211: Scan aborted", then nothing for 90 s), the other only came
back because it also saw INTERFACE_DISABLED/ENABLED.

Ask for a new scan in that case, a second later.

Upstream: to be sent to hostap@lists.infradead.org (not sent yet).
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/events.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/events.c
@@ -2649,6 +2649,15 @@
 	if (data && data->scan_info.aborted) {
 		wpa_dbg(wpa_s, MSG_DEBUG,
 			"Scan was aborted - do not use the incomplete scan results to trigger new operations");
+		/*
+		 * A scan for a network to connect to that was aborted (the
+		 * interface went down and up again under it, as when it joins
+		 * a bond) left the state at SCANNING with nothing to end it:
+		 * no new scan was ever asked for. Ask for one.
+		 */
+		if (own_request && wpa_s->wpa_state == WPA_SCANNING &&
+		    !wpa_s->scan_res_handler)
+			wpa_supplicant_req_new_scan(wpa_s, 1, 0);
 		goto scan_work_done;
 	}
 
